---
import Base from '../../../layouts/Base.astro';
---
<Base noIndex title="Physical Fabric Cutting Check | Quilt Studio" description="Noindex physical ruler recording for matched quilt cutting and purchasing CSVs. User-entered checks are not independent certification.">
 <div class="page-shell qa-fabric-audit" data-qa-fabric-audit>
  <header class="qa-fabric-audit-intro">
   <span class="eyebrow-with-line">— QA LAB / NON-INDEXED, HUMAN MEASUREMENTS REQUIRED</span>
   <h1>Check fabric cuts against your real material</h1>
   <p>Compare cutting instructions with actual fabric width, usable run length and one physically measured sample cut per roll. This is a <strong>local manual self-check</strong>, not automated quality certification.</p>
  </header>
  <section class="qa-fabric-audit-card" aria-labelledby="qa-fabric-load-title">
   <h2 id="qa-fabric-load-title">1. Import the matching project exports</h2>
   <p>On <a href="/calculators/">Project Planner</a>, finish reviewing all actual fabric colors and cutting quantities. Download its <strong>cut-list CSV</strong>, <strong>shopping CSV</strong> and optional <strong>cutting-plan JSON</strong> (for sewn seam checking) from the same calculation. Both files must have the same eight-character project fingerprint and physical roll IDs. Files are read locally in your browser; the site does not upload them.</p>
   <div class="qa-fabric-field-grid">
    <label>Physical cut-list CSV
     <input type="file" data-fabric-cuts accept=".csv,text/csv" aria-describedby="qa-fabric-file-limit" />
    </label>
    <label>Shopping CSV for the same project
     <input type="file" data-fabric-shopping accept=".csv,text/csv" aria-describedby="qa-fabric-file-limit" />
    </label>
    <label>Optional: matching Project Planner cutting-plan JSON (seam checking)
     <input type="file" data-fabric-plan-json accept=".json,application/json" aria-describedby="qa-fabric-file-limit" />
    </label>
   </div>
   <p id="qa-fabric-file-limit" class="qa-fabric-small">Only the site's current 12-column, source-tagged CSV exports are supported; each CSV and optional JSON must be smaller than 2 MB. Without a matching JSON file sewn seams remain UNVERIFIED. A short fingerprint identifies matching revisions, but is <strong>not</strong> a cryptographic signature or proof of file authenticity.</p>
   <button type="button" class="action-primary" data-fabric-import>Check both CSV files</button>
   <div data-fabric-import-status role="status" aria-live="polite">No files imported. No physical cutting evidence has been checked.</div>
  </section>
  <section class="qa-fabric-audit-card" data-fabric-workspace hidden aria-labelledby="qa-fabric-measure-title">
   <h2 id="qa-fabric-measure-title">2. Measure the actual material</h2>
   <p data-fabric-snapshot></p>
   <p>Measure <strong>usable postwash fabric width</strong> after selvedges, and <strong>available usable roll length</strong> along the bolt; these measurements must refer to the same condition as the planned cuts. If you also measured that <em>same fabric length before washing</em>, enter it to calculate the observed shrinkage percentage and compare with the shopping calculation. Pick one physical sample cut per roll. This cannot validate every piece, join or seam.</p>
   <div class="qa-fabric-field-grid">
    <label>Physical measurement date
     <input data-fabric-date type="date" />
    </label>
    <label>Actual fabric condition
     <select data-fabric-condition>
      <option value="">Select condition</option>
      <option value="postwash">Measured after any intended washing/shrinkage</option>
      <option value="not-postwashed">Not washed / condition unsure — inconclusive</option>
     </select>
    </label>
    <label>Allowed sample-cut deviation (inches)
     <input data-fabric-tolerance type="number" min="0" max="0.25" step="any" inputmode="decimal" placeholder="e.g. 0.0625 = 1/16 in" />
    </label>
    <label>Reviewer (optional)
     <input data-fabric-reviewer type="text" maxlength="200" placeholder="Local self-check name" autocomplete="off" />
    </label>
   </div>
   <p class="qa-fabric-small">Enter your own cutting tolerance, from 0 to ¼ inch. There is no single universally approved allowance; your sewing method may require a stricter threshold. For example, 0.0625 = 1/16 inch. Do not treat an allowed deviation as a verified industry specification. <strong>Before-wash length is optional</strong>, but if omitted the site will explicitly state that the real shrinkage rate was not verified. Estimated purchase yardage is checked against the cutting run and modeled shrinkage before any physical results are shown.</p>
   <div data-fabric-rolls></div>
   <section class="qa-fabric-roll" data-fabric-seam-area hidden aria-labelledby="qa-fabric-seam-heading">
    <h3 id="qa-fabric-seam-heading">Optional: measure sewn backing and binding joins</h3>
    <p>First confirm the actual backing seam orientation. For each join, optionally measure its <strong>net length take-up</strong> (lost usable span), then independently measure the <strong>complete joined dimension before trimming</strong>. The tool sums the individual losses and checks them against the separately measured overall length; no value is filled from the model. Measurements are user-reported, not independent certification.</p>
    <div class="qa-fabric-field-grid">
     <label>Allowed total joint loss above model (inches; 0–1)
      <input type="number" min="0" max="1" step="any" inputmode="decimal" data-fabric-seam-tolerance placeholder="e.g. 0.125" />
     </label>
    </div>
    <p class="qa-fabric-small">The allowance applies to the <strong>whole joined assembly</strong>, not each seam. A joined span shorter than required is always flagged. For backing, measure net take-up of the two joined panel edges at each seam; for straight-grain binding, measure the net loss along the strip after each join (diagonal joins do not necessarily equal twice a nominal seam allowance). These checks use the real postwash usable WOF above and do not verify stitch quality or pressing distortion.</p>
    <div data-fabric-seams></div>
   </section>
   <details class="qa-fabric-roll" data-fabric-finishing-area hidden>
    <summary>Optional: actual four-edge backing trim and sewn quilt-top outside size</summary>
    <p class="qa-fabric-small" data-fabric-finishing-plan></p>
    <p>Use a ruler to record assembled backing dimensions BEFORE trimming, actual fabric removed from EACH of four edges, and independently measured backing dimensions AFTER trimming. Separately measure the sewn quilt TOP outside before batting, quilting and binding. <strong>All values start blank</strong>, and this never certifies the final bound quilt.</p>
    <div class="qa-fabric-field-grid">
     <label>User-declared finishing tolerance (0–1 inch)
      <input type="number" min="0" max="1" step="any" data-fabric-finishing-tolerance placeholder="e.g. 0.0625" />
     </label>
     <label>Untrimmed backing width (inches)
      <input type="number" min="0" step="any" data-fabric-finish="pretrimBackingWidthIn" />
     </label>
     <label>Untrimmed backing height (inches)
      <input type="number" min="0" step="any" data-fabric-finish="pretrimBackingHeightIn" />
     </label>
     <label>Backing LEFT edge removed (inches; zero allowed)
      <input type="number" min="0" step="any" data-fabric-finish="trimLeftIn" />
     </label>
     <label>Backing RIGHT edge removed (inches; zero allowed)
      <input type="number" min="0" step="any" data-fabric-finish="trimRightIn" />
     </label>
     <label>Backing TOP edge removed (inches; zero allowed)
      <input type="number" min="0" step="any" data-fabric-finish="trimTopIn" />
     </label>
     <label>Backing BOTTOM edge removed (inches; zero allowed)
      <input type="number" min="0" step="any" data-fabric-finish="trimBottomIn" />
     </label>
     <label>Independent backing width AFTER trimming (inches)
      <input type="number" min="0" step="any" data-fabric-finish="trimmedBackingWidthIn" />
     </label>
     <label>Independent backing height AFTER trimming (inches)
      <input type="number" min="0" step="any" data-fabric-finish="trimmedBackingHeightIn" />
     </label>
     <label>Sewn quilt TOP outside width BEFORE quilting (inches)
      <input type="number" min="0" step="any" data-fabric-finish="sewnQuiltTopWidthIn" />
     </label>
     <label>Sewn quilt TOP outside height BEFORE quilting (inches)
      <input type="number" min="0" step="any" data-fabric-finish="sewnQuiltTopHeightIn" />
     </label>
    </div>
    <p class="qa-fabric-small">Removing four backing edges and independently measuring the resulting dimensions are separate checks; a partially filled checklist stays unverified. Backing below its required size is always flagged regardless of tolerance.</p>
    <div data-fabric-finishing-result role="status" aria-live="polite">Finishing measurements NOT VERIFIED.</div>
   </details>
   <details class="qa-fabric-roll" data-top-chain-area hidden>
    <summary>Optional: manually ordered quilt-TOP seam chain — physical pieces to a sewn row or column</summary>
    <p class="qa-fabric-small" data-top-chain-plan></p>
    <p>Quilt-top cut-list CSV pieces have <strong>NO sewn placement/order</strong>. Select physical fabric pieces in your real sewn order; enter each piece's actual cut span along the chosen axis, and the <strong>net physical length consumed on both joining edges</strong> at each straight butt seam. Compare with a separately ruler-measured assembled chain before borders. No ruler values are prefilled; diagonal or overlap joins are not modeled here.</p>
    <div class="qa-fabric-field-grid">
     <label>Actual chain direction
      <select data-top-chain-axis>
       <option value="">Select width or height (required)</option>
       <option value="width">Width — one horizontal row</option>
       <option value="height">Height — one vertical column</option>
      </select>
     </label>
     <label>Number of consecutive physical pieces (2–12)
      <input type="number" data-top-chain-count min="2" max="12" step="1" value="2" />
     </label>
     <label>User-declared TOTAL chain dimensional tolerance (0–1 inch)
      <input data-top-chain-tolerance type="number" min="0" max="1" step="any" placeholder="e.g. 0.0625" />
     </label>
     <label>Independently measured sewn chain span BEFORE borders (inches)
      <input data-top-chain-joined type="number" min="0" step="any" placeholder="Actual ruler measurement" />
     </label>
    </div>
    <label class="qa-fabric-confirm">
     <input type="checkbox" data-top-chain-full-center />
     This exact chain spans the COMPLETE quilt TOP CENTER before borders. Only if checked may it be compared with the model center width/height. An arbitrary row/column cannot prove whole-top construction.
    </label>
    <div class="qa-fabric-buttons">
     <button type="button" class="header-cta" data-top-chain-create>Create blank chain from count</button>
     <button type="button" class="header-cta" data-top-chain-clear>Clear this chain</button>
    </div>
    <div data-top-chain-pieces></div>
    <div data-top-chain-joins></div>
    <p class="qa-fabric-small">For each piece, choose its physical fabric SKU and printed cut-list piece number, then measure the actual cut span. For every join, measure the lost length at the previous piece's trailing edge and the next piece's leading edge (zero allowed). The listed cut dimensions are only reference data, never automatically treated as actual measurements.</p>
    <div data-top-chain-result role="status" aria-live="polite">No real quilt-top seam chain reported: NOT VERIFIED.</div>
   </details>
   <label class="qa-fabric-confirm"><input type="checkbox" data-fabric-confirm /> I actually measured the fabric and sample cuts with a physical ruler. I understand that browser and CSV calculations cannot independently verify my statements.</label>
   <h2>3. Review the user-reported results</h2>
   <div data-fabric-result role="status" aria-live="polite">No physical measurements entered.</div>
   <div class="qa-fabric-buttons">
    <button type="button" class="action-primary" data-fabric-download disabled>Download local user-reported evidence JSON</button>
    <button type="button" class="header-cta" data-fabric-reset>Clear measurements and imported files</button>
   </div>
   <p class="qa-fabric-small"><strong>Important:</strong> Within-limit results never mean an independent physical PASS. A complete failed or inconclusive self-check remains exportable so negative evidence is preserved. The site never sends, saves or certifies your files or measurements.</p>
  </section>
  <nav class="qa-fabric-audit-card" aria-label="Further physical QA">
   <h2>Physical verification remains separate</h2>
   <p>For real paper scaling, use the <a href="/qa/print-calibration/">noindex printer ruler worksheet</a>. The physical cutting release gate remains <strong>MANUAL_NOT_RUN</strong> pending qualified human review, real materials and separately recorded seam results. A project fingerprint is not a substitute.</p>
   <a class="header-cta" href="/calculators/">Back to Project Planner</a>
  </nav>
 </div>
 <script>
  import {
   importFabricAudit,assessFabricAudit,fabricAuditEvidence,
   type ImportedFabricAudit,type ManualFabricAuditInput,type ManualRollReading,
   type FabricAuditRoll
  } from '../../../lib/quilt/fabric-audit';
  import {readJoinedSeamPlan,type PlannedSeamCheck} from '../../../lib/quilt/seam-audit';
  import type {UserFinishingReading} from '../../../lib/quilt/finishing-audit';
  import type {UserTopChain} from '../../../lib/quilt/top-chain-audit';
  const parent=document.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-qa-fabric-audit]');
  const cutsFile=parent?.querySelector<HTMLInputElement>('[data-fabric-cuts]');
  const shoppingFile=parent?.querySelector<HTMLInputElement>('[data-fabric-shopping]');
  const planJsonFile=parent?.querySelector<HTMLInputElement>('[data-fabric-plan-json]');
  const importButton=parent?.querySelector<HTMLButtonElement>('[data-fabric-import]');
  const importStatus=parent?.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-fabric-import-status]');
  const workspace=parent?.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-fabric-workspace]');
  const rollsContainer=parent?.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-fabric-rolls]');
  const seamArea=parent?.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-fabric-seam-area]');
  const seamContainer=parent?.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-fabric-seams]');
  const finishArea=parent?.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-fabric-finishing-area]');
  const finishPlan=parent?.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-fabric-finishing-plan]');
  const finishResult=parent?.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-fabric-finishing-result]');
  const topArea=parent?.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-top-chain-area]');
  const topPlan=parent?.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-top-chain-plan]');
  const topPieces=parent?.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-top-chain-pieces]');
  const topJoins=parent?.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-top-chain-joins]');
  const topResult=parent?.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-top-chain-result]');
  const topCreate=parent?.querySelector<HTMLButtonElement>('[data-top-chain-create]');
  const topClear=parent?.querySelector<HTMLButtonElement>('[data-top-chain-clear]');
  const snapshot=parent?.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-fabric-snapshot]');
  const resultNode=parent?.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-fabric-result]');
  const exportButton=parent?.querySelector<HTMLButtonElement>('[data-fabric-download]');
  const resetButton=parent?.querySelector<HTMLButtonElement>('[data-fabric-reset]');
  let imported:ImportedFabricAudit|null=null;
  let attempt=0;
  const query=<T extends Element>(selector:string)=>parent?.querySelector<T>(selector)??null;
  const fieldValue=(selector:string)=>query<HTMLInputElement|HTMLSelectElement>(selector)?.value??'';
  const numberValue=(el:HTMLInputElement|null)=>el?.value.trim()?Number(el.value):undefined;
  function labelFor(value:string):HTMLLabelElement{
   const label=document.createElement('label');label.textContent=value;return label;
  }
  function numericField(title:string,field:string):HTMLLabelElement{
   const label=labelFor(title);
   const input=document.createElement('input');
   input.type='number';input.step='any';input.min='0.00001';input.max='100000';
   input.inputMode='decimal';input.dataset.measurement=field;
   label.appendChild(input);return label;
  }
  function rollForm(roll:FabricAuditRoll):HTMLElement{
   const block=document.createElement('section');block.className='qa-fabric-roll';block.dataset.fabricRollId=roll.id;
   const heading=document.createElement('h3');heading.textContent=roll.material+' · '+roll.id;
   const summary=document.createElement('p');
   summary.textContent=roll.pieces.length+' cut pieces · required usable WOF '+roll.usableWofIn+' in · full roll cut run '+roll.requiredRunIn+' in · modeled length shrinkage '+(roll.plannedLengthShrinkagePct??0).toFixed(2)+'% · exact prewash '+(roll.plannedRawPurchaseYards??0).toFixed(4)+' yd · rounded purchase '+(roll.plannedRoundedPurchaseYards??0).toFixed(4)+' yd';
   const grid=document.createElement('div');grid.className='qa-fabric-field-grid';
   grid.append(numericField('Real usable WOF after intended washing (inches)','wof'),numericField('Real usable run length after intended washing (inches)','run'),
    numericField('Actual before-wash length of SAME roll segment (inches; optional)','prewash'));
   const pick=labelFor('Which physical cut did you sample?');
   const select=document.createElement('select');select.dataset.measurement='piece';
   for(const piece of roll.pieces){
    const option=document.createElement('option');
    option.value=String(piece.pieceNumber);
    option.textContent='#'+piece.pieceNumber+' · '+piece.label+' · '+piece.widthIn+' × '+piece.heightIn+' in';
    select.appendChild(option);
   }
   pick.appendChild(select);
   grid.append(pick,numericField('Measured sample cut width (inches)','width'),
    numericField('Measured sample cut height (inches)','height'));
   const line=document.createElement('p');line.className='qa-fabric-small';line.dataset.measurementResult='';
   line.textContent='No real measurements recorded for this fabric roll.';
   block.append(heading,summary,grid,line);
   return block;
  }
  function seamForm(spec:PlannedSeamCheck):HTMLElement{
   const block=document.createElement('section');block.className='qa-fabric-seam-item';
   block.dataset.fabricSeamKind=spec.kind;
   const heading=document.createElement('h4');
   heading.textContent=spec.kind==='backing'
    ?'Backing · '+spec.direction+' seams · '+spec.sectionCount+' panels'
    :'Straight-grain binding · '+spec.sectionCount+' strips';
   const expected=document.createElement('p');expected.className='qa-fabric-small';
   expected.textContent='Expected before trimming: '+spec.plannedPretrimJoinedLengthIn.toFixed(3)+
    ' in joined, at least '+spec.requiredMinimumLengthIn.toFixed(3)+' in required. '+spec.joinCount+
    ' joins; planned total seam loss '+spec.modeledTotalJoinLossIn.toFixed(3)+' in.';
   block.append(heading,expected);
   if(spec.joinCount>0){
    if(spec.kind==='backing'){
     const directionLabel=labelFor('Observed direction of sewn backing panel seams (optional)');
     const direction=document.createElement('select');direction.dataset.fabricObservedDirection='';
     const options=[
      {value:'',title:'Not physically confirmed'},
      {value:'vertical',title:'Vertical seams'},
      {value:'horizontal',title:'Horizontal seams'}
     ];
     for(const item of options){
      const option=document.createElement('option');option.value=item.value;
      option.textContent=item.title;direction.appendChild(option);
     }
     directionLabel.appendChild(direction);block.append(directionLabel);
    }
    const label=numericField('Actual complete joined '+spec.kind+' span BEFORE trimming (inches; optional)','joined');
    const measure=label.querySelector('input');
    if(measure)measure.dataset.fabricJoinedMeasurement='';
    block.append(label);
    if(spec.joinCount<=64){
     const detail=document.createElement('details');
     detail.className='qa-fabric-individual-joins';
     const title=document.createElement('summary');
     title.textContent='Optional: record each of the '+spec.joinCount+' join losses, in physical assembly order';
     detail.appendChild(title);
     const grid=document.createElement('div');grid.className='qa-fabric-join-grid';
     for(let i=0;i<spec.joinCount;i++){
      const field=numericField('Join #'+(i+1)+' net length take-up (in; optional)','individual');
      const input=field.querySelector('input');
      if(input){input.min='0';input.dataset.fabricJoinIndex=String(i);}
      grid.appendChild(field);
     }
     detail.appendChild(grid);
     const hint=document.createElement('p');hint.className='qa-fabric-small';
     hint.textContent='Blank joints remain NOT MEASURED. All '+spec.joinCount+' are required before cumulative join loss is considered complete. Exact zero is allowed; no example measurements are prefilled.';
     detail.appendChild(hint);block.append(detail);
    }else{
     const note=document.createElement('p');note.className='qa-fabric-small';
     note.textContent='More than 64 joins: record them outside the browser; only the whole assembled length can be entered here. Per-join loss remains unverified.';
     block.append(note);
    }
   }else{
    const text=document.createElement('p');text.className='qa-fabric-small';
    text.textContent='One section, no seam join to verify.';
    block.append(text);
   }
   const assessment=document.createElement('p');assessment.dataset.fabricSeamResult='';
   assessment.className='qa-fabric-small';assessment.textContent='No real sewn dimension measured.';
   block.append(assessment);
   return block;
  }
  function createTopChainRows():void{
   if(!imported?.seamPlan||!topPieces||!topJoins)return;
   const count=Number(fieldValue('[data-top-chain-count]'));
   if(!Number.isSafeInteger(count)||count<2||count>12){
    if(topResult)topResult.textContent='Select a whole piece count between 2 and 12; nothing has been measured.';
    return;
   }
   const sourceRolls=imported.rolls.filter(r=>r.id.startsWith('fabric:')&&r.pieces.length>0);
   if(!sourceRolls.length){
    if(topResult)topResult.textContent='No physical quilt-top fabric cut-list pieces. This check is unavailable.';
    return;
   }
   const pieces:HTMLElement[]=[],joins:HTMLElement[]=[];
   for(let i=0;i<count;i++){
    const row=document.createElement('section');row.className='qa-top-chain-row';
    row.dataset.topChainPiece=String(i);
    const h=document.createElement('h4');h.textContent='Sewn position #'+(i+1)+' (actual quilt TOP cut piece)';
    const grid=document.createElement('div');grid.className='qa-fabric-field-grid';
    const rollLabel=labelFor('Physical fabric SKU for piece #'+(i+1));
    const select=document.createElement('select');select.dataset.topChainRoll='';
    const empty=document.createElement('option');empty.value='';empty.textContent='Choose the actual cut-list fabric roll';
    select.append(empty);
    for(const roll of sourceRolls){
     const opt=document.createElement('option');opt.value=roll.id;
     opt.textContent=roll.material+' · '+roll.id+' ('+roll.pieces.length+' numbered cuts)';
     select.append(opt);
    }
    rollLabel.append(select);
    const numberLabel=numericField('Printed cut-list piece number at sewn position #'+(i+1),'chainPieceNum');
    const num=numberLabel.querySelector('input');
    if(num){num.dataset.topChainPieceNum='';num.step='1';num.min='1';num.max='2000';}
    const measureLabel=numericField('ACTUALLY measured span along this chain (inches)','chainCutSpan');
    const measure=measureLabel.querySelector('input');
    if(measure)measure.dataset.topChainCutSpan='';
    grid.append(rollLabel,numberLabel,measureLabel);
    const hint=document.createElement('p');hint.className='qa-fabric-small';hint.dataset.topChainPieceInfo='';
    hint.textContent='No source cut piece chosen; actual ruler span NOT MEASURED.';
    row.append(h,grid,hint);pieces.push(row);
    if(i<count-1){
     const joined=document.createElement('section');joined.className='qa-top-chain-row';
     joined.dataset.topChainJoin=String(i);
     const title=document.createElement('h4');title.textContent='Physical straight butt join #'+(i+1)+': position '+(i+1)+' to '+(i+2);
     const fields=document.createElement('div');fields.className='qa-fabric-field-grid';
     const last=numericField('Consumed length from previous piece edge (inches)','chainLossPrevious');
     const first=numericField('Consumed length from next piece edge (inches)','chainLossNext');
     const left=last.querySelector('input'),right=first.querySelector('input');
     if(left){left.min='0';left.dataset.topChainLossPrevious='';}
     if(right){right.min='0';right.dataset.topChainLossNext='';}
     fields.append(last,first);
     joined.append(title,fields);joins.push(joined);
    }
   }
   topPieces.replaceChildren(...pieces);topJoins.replaceChildren(...joins);
   if(topResult)topResult.textContent='Blank chain created. Select real cut pieces and enter independent ruler readings; NOT VERIFIED until recorded.';
   render();
  }
  function readManual():ManualFabricAuditInput|null{
   if(!imported)return null;
   const readings:ManualRollReading[]=[];
   for(const roll of rollsContainer?.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-fabric-roll-id]')??[]){
    const el=<T extends Element>(role:string)=>roll.querySelector<T>('[data-measurement="'+role+'"]');
    readings.push({
     id:roll.dataset.fabricRollId??'',
     actualUsableWofIn:numberValue(el<HTMLInputElement>('wof')),
     actualUsableRunIn:numberValue(el<HTMLInputElement>('run')),
     measuredPrewashRunIn:numberValue(el<HTMLInputElement>('prewash')),
     sampledPieceNumber:Number(el<HTMLSelectElement>('piece')?.value),
     measuredPieceWidthIn:numberValue(el<HTMLInputElement>('width')),
     measuredPieceHeightIn:numberValue(el<HTMLInputElement>('height'))
    });
   }
   const joinedSeamReadings=[...(seamContainer?.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-fabric-seam-kind]')??[])]
    .filter(item=>item.querySelector('[data-fabric-joined-measurement]'))
    .map(item=>{
     const jointInputs=[...item.querySelectorAll<HTMLInputElement>('[data-fabric-join-index]')];
     const direction=item.querySelector<HTMLSelectElement>('[data-fabric-observed-direction]')?.value;
     return {
      kind:item.dataset.fabricSeamKind as 'backing'|'binding',
      measuredPretrimJoinedLengthIn:numberValue(item.querySelector<HTMLInputElement>('[data-fabric-joined-measurement]')),
      observedBackingJoinDirection:direction ? direction as 'vertical'|'horizontal' : undefined,
      perJoinObservedLossesIn:jointInputs.length?jointInputs.map(input=>numberValue(input)):undefined
     };
    });
   const fields=[
    'pretrimBackingWidthIn','pretrimBackingHeightIn',
    'trimLeftIn','trimRightIn','trimTopIn','trimBottomIn',
    'trimmedBackingWidthIn','trimmedBackingHeightIn',
    'sewnQuiltTopWidthIn','sewnQuiltTopHeightIn'
   ] as const;
   const finishingReading:UserFinishingReading={};
   for(const key of fields){
    const value=numberValue(query<HTMLInputElement>('[data-fabric-finish="'+key+'"]'));
    if(value!==undefined)finishingReading[key]=value;
   }
   const selectedPieces=[...(topPieces?.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-top-chain-piece]')??[])];
   const selectedJoins=[...(topJoins?.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-top-chain-join]')??[])];
   const topChain:UserTopChain|undefined=selectedPieces.length?{
    axis:fieldValue('[data-top-chain-axis]') as UserTopChain['axis'],
    spansEntireCenter:query<HTMLInputElement>('[data-top-chain-full-center]')?.checked??false,
    declaredTotalToleranceIn:numberValue(query<HTMLInputElement>('[data-top-chain-tolerance]')),
    observedJoinedSpanIn:numberValue(query<HTMLInputElement>('[data-top-chain-joined]')),
    pieces:selectedPieces.map(row=>({
     rollId:row.querySelector<HTMLSelectElement>('[data-top-chain-roll]')?.value??'',
     pieceNumber:numberValue(row.querySelector<HTMLInputElement>('[data-top-chain-piece-num]'))??0,
     observedCutSpanIn:numberValue(row.querySelector<HTMLInputElement>('[data-top-chain-cut-span]'))
    })),
    joins:selectedJoins.map(row=>({
     previousEdgeTakeupIn:numberValue(row.querySelector<HTMLInputElement>('[data-top-chain-loss-previous]')),
     nextEdgeTakeupIn:numberValue(row.querySelector<HTMLInputElement>('[data-top-chain-loss-next]'))
    }))
   }:undefined;
   return {
    project:imported,readings,
    topChain,joinedSeamReadings,
    allowedSeamDeviationIn:numberValue(query<HTMLInputElement>('[data-fabric-seam-tolerance]')),
    finishingReading,allowedFinishingDeviationIn:numberValue(query<HTMLInputElement>('[data-fabric-finishing-tolerance]')),
    date:fieldValue('[data-fabric-date]'),
    fabricCondition:fieldValue('[data-fabric-condition]') as ManualFabricAuditInput['fabricCondition'],
    allowedPieceDeviationIn:numberValue(query<HTMLInputElement>('[data-fabric-tolerance]')),
    reviewer:fieldValue('[data-fabric-reviewer]'),
    physicallyMeasured:query<HTMLInputElement>('[data-fabric-confirm]')?.checked??false
   };
  }
  function render():void{
   const input=readManual();if(!input||!resultNode||!exportButton)return;
   const outcome=assessFabricAudit(input);
   resultNode.dataset.fabricAssessment=outcome.status;
   resultNode.textContent=outcome.message+(outcome.missing.length?' Missing: '+outcome.missing.join('; ')+'.':'');
   exportButton.disabled=!outcome.canExport;
   const chain=outcome.topChainCheck;
   if(topResult){
    topResult.dataset.topChainCoverage=chain.coverage;
    const notes=[
     'Top chain: '+chain.coverage+'. Source: '+chain.source+'.',
     'User-selected physical cuts '+chain.recordedPieceCount+'/'+chain.cutPieceCount+
      ', measured joining edges '+chain.recordedJoinEdgeCount+'/'+(chain.joinCount*2)+'.'
    ];
    if(chain.measuredCutSpanSumIn!==undefined)
     notes.push('Total ACTUAL cut spans '+chain.measuredCutSpanSumIn.toFixed(3)+' in.');
    if(chain.summedNetSeamTakeupIn!==undefined)
     notes.push('Two-sided measured seam losses summed '+chain.summedNetSeamTakeupIn.toFixed(3)+' in.');
    if(chain.predictedJoinedSpanFromMeasuredPartsIn!==undefined)
     notes.push('Predicted assembled span from ACTUAL cuts − ACTUAL seam edges '+
      chain.predictedJoinedSpanFromMeasuredPartsIn.toFixed(3)+' in.');
    if(chain.joinedSpanDifferenceIn!==undefined)
     notes.push('Independent joined-span ruler minus predicted '+chain.joinedSpanDifferenceIn.toFixed(3)+' in.');
    if(chain.centerSpanDifferenceIn!==undefined)
     notes.push('User-claimed complete CENTER chain vs planned center difference '+
      chain.centerSpanDifferenceIn.toFixed(3)+' in.');
    if(chain.cutSizeDeviationCount>0)
     notes.push(chain.cutSizeDeviationCount+' selected real cut spans outside native CSV size tolerance.');
    notes.push(...chain.warnings);
    if(chain.invalid.length)notes.push('Invalid: '+chain.invalid.join('; '));
    topResult.textContent=notes.join(' ')+' All physical results USER REPORTED; NOT independent quilt-top verification.';
    for(const row of topPieces?.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-top-chain-piece]')??[]){
     const info=row.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-top-chain-piece-info]');
     if(!info)continue;
     const rid=row.querySelector<HTMLSelectElement>('[data-top-chain-roll]')?.value??'';
     const pieceNo=numberValue(row.querySelector<HTMLInputElement>('[data-top-chain-piece-num]'));
     const piece=imported?.rolls.find(x=>x.id===rid)?.pieces.find(x=>x.pieceNumber===pieceNo);
     const axis=fieldValue('[data-top-chain-axis]');
     info.textContent=piece?
      'Reference CSV cut #'+pieceNo+': width '+piece.widthIn+' × height '+piece.heightIn+
       ' in; expected '+axis+' span '+(axis==='width'?piece.widthIn:piece.heightIn)+
       ' in. This is NOT the real measured span.':
      'Select an actual fabric SKU and valid physical cut-list piece number; ruler span NOT inferred.';
    }
   }
   const finish=outcome.finishingCheck;
   if(finishResult){
    finishResult.dataset.fabricFinishingCoverage=finish.backingCoverage;
    const parts=[
     'Backing four-edge measurement: '+finish.backingCoverage+'.',
     'Sewn quilt TOP outside measurement: '+finish.topCoverage+'.'
    ];
    if(finish.impliedTrimmedBackingWidthIn!==undefined){
     parts.push('Backing after four edge removals should be '+
      finish.impliedTrimmedBackingWidthIn.toFixed(3)+' × '+
      finish.impliedTrimmedBackingHeightIn?.toFixed(3)+' in. '+
      'Independent posttrim width difference '+finish.trimmedWidthDifferenceIn?.toFixed(3)+
      ' in, height difference '+finish.trimmedHeightDifferenceIn?.toFixed(3)+
      ' in, removed area '+finish.observedTrimAreaSqIn?.toFixed(2)+' sq in.');
    }
    if(finish.joinedPretrimAxisDifferenceIn!==undefined)
     parts.push('Backing pretrim versus whole joined seam span discrepancy '+
      finish.joinedPretrimAxisDifferenceIn.toFixed(3)+' in.');
    if(finish.sewnTopWidthDifferenceIn!==undefined)
     parts.push('Sewn quilt TOP vs plan differences: '+
      finish.sewnTopWidthDifferenceIn.toFixed(3)+' in width and '+
      finish.sewnTopHeightDifferenceIn?.toFixed(3)+' in height.');
    parts.push(...finish.warnings);
    if(finish.invalid.length)parts.push('Invalid: '+finish.invalid.join('; '));
    parts.push('User reported only; physical dimensions after quilting/binding NOT VERIFIED.');
    finishResult.textContent=parts.join(' ');
   }
   for(const check of outcome.seamChecks){
    const node=[...(seamContainer?.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-fabric-seam-kind]')??[])]
     .find(el=>el.dataset.fabricSeamKind===check.kind)?.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-fabric-seam-result]');
    if(!node)continue;
    if(check.joinCount===0){node.textContent='No sewn seam to verify.';continue;}
    const notes:string[]=[];
    if(check.kind==='backing'){
     notes.push(check.observedBackingJoinDirection?
      'Actual sewn backing seams: '+check.observedBackingJoinDirection+'.':
      'Actual backing seam direction NOT CONFIRMED.');
     if(check.backingDirectionMismatch)notes.push('SEAM DIRECTION DOES NOT MATCH THE PLAN.');
    }
    notes.push(check.measuredPretrimJoinedLengthIn===undefined?
     'No full joined span measured: NOT VERIFIED.':
     'Reported pretrim joined span '+check.measuredPretrimJoinedLengthIn.toFixed(3)+
      ' in; observed total loss '+check.observedTotalJoinLossIn?.toFixed(3)+
      ' in versus modeled '+check.modeledTotalJoinLossIn.toFixed(3)+' in.');
    notes.push('Individually measured joins: '+check.perJoinMeasuredCount+'/'+check.joinCount+'.');
    if(check.perJoinTotalLossIn!==undefined){
     notes.push('SUM of actual per-join losses: '+check.perJoinTotalLossIn.toFixed(3)+
      ' in; predicted assembled span '+check.predictedJoinedSpanFromPerJoinIn?.toFixed(3)+' in.');
     if(check.perJoinLossExceedsModel)notes.push('CUMULATIVE JOIN LOSS EXCEEDS PLANNED TOTAL.');
     if(check.perJoinVsAssembledSpanDifferenceIn!==undefined){
      notes.push('Independent whole-span minus per-join prediction: '+
       check.perJoinVsAssembledSpanDifferenceIn.toFixed(3)+' in.');
      if(check.perJoinVsAssembledSpanMismatch)notes.push('PER-JOIN AND WHOLE-SPAN MEASUREMENTS DISAGREE.');
     }
    }else notes.push('Full per-join take-up NOT VERIFIED.');
    if(check.assembledSpanShortfall)notes.push('SHORTER THAN REQUIRED FINISHED SPAN.');
    if(check.observedLossExceedsModel)notes.push('JOIN LOSS EXCEEDS ASSUMED TOTAL.');
    notes.push('User-reported measurements only; never an independent physical pass.');
    node.textContent=notes.join(' ');
   }
   for(const check of outcome.checks){
    const node=[...(rollsContainer?.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-fabric-roll-id]')??[])]
     .find(el=>el.dataset.fabricRollId===check.id)?.querySelector<HTMLElement>('[data-measurement-result]');
    if(!node)continue;
    if(check.actualUsableWofIn===undefined||check.widthDifferenceIn===undefined){
     node.textContent='This roll still needs real usable width/length and one measured sample piece.';continue;
    }
    node.textContent='WOF '+check.actualUsableWofIn+' vs '+check.requiredWofIn+
     ' in; run '+check.actualUsableRunIn+' vs '+check.requiredRunIn+
     ' in; sampled piece #'+check.sampledPieceNumber+' width difference '+check.widthDifferenceIn?.toFixed(4)+
     ' in, height difference '+check.heightDifferenceIn?.toFixed(4)+' in. '+
     (check.hasShortage?'REPORTED SHORTAGE. ':'')+
     (check.sampleOutsideAllowance?'SAMPLE EXCEEDS ALLOWANCE. ':'')+
     (check.observedLengthShrinkagePct===undefined?
      'Before-wash length not entered; observed shrinkage is unverified.':
      ' Observed length shrinkage '+check.observedLengthShrinkagePct.toFixed(2)+
      '% vs modeled '+(check.plannedLengthShrinkagePct??0).toFixed(2)+'%. '+
      (check.observedShrinkageExceedsPlan?'EXCEEDS PLANNED SHRINKAGE.':'Within modeled rate.'));
   }
  }
  async function load():Promise<void>{
   const current=++attempt;
   imported=null;
   if(workspace)workspace.hidden=true;
   if(exportButton)exportButton.disabled=true;
   if(!cutsFile?.files?.length||!shoppingFile?.files?.length){
    if(importStatus)importStatus.textContent='Choose both the cut-list CSV and the shopping CSV from one saved calculation.';
    return;
   }
   const cutFile=cutsFile.files[0],shopFile=shoppingFile.files[0];
   const extraFile=planJsonFile?.files?.[0];
   if(cutFile.size>2_000_000||shopFile.size>2_000_000||(extraFile&&extraFile.size>2_000_000)){
    if(importStatus)importStatus.textContent='Each CSV must be smaller than 2 MB.';return;
   }
   if(importStatus)importStatus.textContent='Reading both CSV files locally…';
   try{
    const [cuts,shop,sidecar]=await Promise.all([cutFile.text(),shopFile.text(),extraFile?extraFile.text():Promise.resolve(undefined)]);
    if(current!==attempt)return;
    const parsed=importFabricAudit(cuts,shop);
    if(sidecar!==undefined)parsed.seamPlan=readJoinedSeamPlan(parsed,sidecar);
    imported=parsed;
    rollsContainer?.replaceChildren(...parsed.rolls.map(rollForm));
    seamContainer?.replaceChildren(...(parsed.seamPlan?.checks??[]).map(seamForm));
    if(seamArea)seamArea.hidden=!parsed.seamPlan;
    if(finishArea){finishArea.hidden=!parsed.seamPlan;finishArea.removeAttribute('open');}
    if(finishPlan&&parsed.seamPlan){
     const expected=parsed.seamPlan.finishing;
     finishPlan.textContent='Plan: sewn quilt TOP outside '+expected.plannedQuiltTopWidthIn+' × '+
      expected.plannedQuiltTopHeightIn+' in; backing AFTER trim at least '+
      expected.requiredBackingWidthIn+' × '+expected.requiredBackingHeightIn+' in. '+
      'Model backing BEFORE trimming '+expected.plannedPretrimBackingWidthIn+' × '+
      expected.plannedPretrimBackingHeightIn+' in. These targets are NOT physical measurements.';
    }
    if(snapshot)snapshot.textContent='Matched snapshot '+parsed.sourceProjectHash+' · '+parsed.rolls.length+' separate rolls · '+parsed.cutCount+' physical cuts. This tag is only a short consistency marker.';
    if(workspace)workspace.hidden=false;
    if(importStatus)importStatus.textContent='Both CSVs match by project revision, roll IDs and geometry. '+(parsed.seamPlan?'The cutting-plan JSON also reconciles with the backing and binding cut pieces.':'No cutting-plan JSON: sewn seams remain UNVERIFIED.')+' Physical measurements have not yet been performed.';
    render();
   }catch(error){
    if(current!==attempt)return;
    imported=null;
    if(importStatus)importStatus.textContent='CSV or optional JSON validation rejected: '+(error instanceof Error?error.message:String(error));
    if(workspace)workspace.hidden=true;
   }
  }
  importButton?.addEventListener('click',()=>{void load();});
  workspace?.addEventListener('input',render);
  workspace?.addEventListener('change',render);
  resetButton?.addEventListener('click',()=>{
   ++attempt;imported=null;if(cutsFile)cutsFile.value='';if(shoppingFile)shoppingFile.value='';if(planJsonFile)planJsonFile.value='';
   for(const selector of ['[data-fabric-date]','[data-fabric-tolerance]','[data-fabric-seam-tolerance]','[data-fabric-finishing-tolerance]','[data-fabric-reviewer]']){
    const input=query<HTMLInputElement>(selector);if(input)input.value='';
   }
   const condition=query<HTMLSelectElement>('[data-fabric-condition]');if(condition)condition.value='';
   const checked=query<HTMLInputElement>('[data-fabric-confirm]');if(checked)checked.checked=false;
   for(const input of finishArea?.querySelectorAll<HTMLInputElement>('[data-fabric-finish]')??[])input.value='';
   rollsContainer?.replaceChildren();seamContainer?.replaceChildren();
   if(seamArea)seamArea.hidden=true;
   if(finishArea){finishArea.hidden=true;finishArea.removeAttribute('open');}
   if(workspace)workspace.hidden=true;
   if(exportButton)exportButton.disabled=true;
   if(importStatus)importStatus.textContent='Cleared. Import a fresh matching pair of CSV files to start again.';
  });
  exportButton?.addEventListener('click',()=>{
   const input=readManual();if(!input||!assessFabricAudit(input).canExport)return;
   const record=fabricAuditEvidence(input,new Date().toISOString());
   const blob=new Blob([JSON.stringify(record,null,2)+'\n'],{type:'application/json'});
   const url=URL.createObjectURL(blob),a=document.createElement('a');
   a.href=url;a.download='quilt-user-reported-fabric-audit-'+record.projectFingerprint+'-'+record.measuredOn+'.json';
   document.body.appendChild(a);a.click();a.remove();setTimeout(()=>URL.revokeObjectURL(url),1500);
  });
 </script>
